Humans in memories are tricky things. The psychic impressions only record what
actually happened; everything else is happening inside your head, as your brain
fills in how things [0m[4mought[0m to work.

But people are harder to predict than spears and doors. If you do much of
anything beyond looking at them, they get hazy and indistinct. You’re hoping to
find a way to fix this, eventually.

