[0m[1mHouse[0m
Or perhaps “entrance hall” would be a better term. The room isn’t large, but the
floor is nicely-smoothed clay, the walls painted with abstract <designs> in red
and blue. By Iron Age standards, whoever lived here must have been distinctly
well off. The passage to the west is indistinct, but has a feeling of motion in
its haziness.

